---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactBanner from '../components/ContactBanner.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../components/SectionLabel.astro';
const principles = [
  ['01','Start with the buying decision.','Before colour palettes or animation, we ask what the visitor needs to understand, believe, and do. That keeps the work commercially honest.'],
  ['02','Make the specific impossible to miss.','Real process, real expertise, real proof, and clear boundaries are more persuasive than inflated claims. We look for the details only your business can say.'],
  ['03','Design earns attention. Clarity earns action.','Distinctive work matters, but it must carry the message rather than compete with it. Every interaction should help the visitor move.'],
  ['04','Own the result together.','You know the customer and the work. We bring strategy, copy, design, development, and growth thinking. The strongest decisions use both sides.']
];
---
<BaseLayout title="About Our Web Design & Growth Studio" description="Meet PressPixel Creations, a web design and digital growth studio helping service businesses turn their expertise into clearer journeys, stronger trust, and qualified enquiries.">
<main id="main" class="studio-page">
  <section class="wrap studio-hero"><SectionLabel>THE THINKING BEHIND PRESSPIXEL</SectionLabel><h1><span class="title-line"><span>Design with taste.</span></span><span class="title-line"><span>Strategy with <em>teeth.</em></span></span></h1><div class="studio-hero-bottom"><p>We help service businesses turn what makes them genuinely good into a digital experience buyers can understand, trust, and act on.</p><span>COMMERCIAL CLARITY<br/>CREATIVE CRAFT</span></div></section>
  <section class="studio-statement"><div class="wrap"><span class="oversized-asterisk" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="asterisk" strokeWidth={1}/></span><SectionLabel>OUR POINT OF VIEW</SectionLabel><h2>Pretty is useful.<br/>But pretty is not a <em>business model.</em></h2><div class="studio-copy"><p>A visitor does not owe a website their attention. They arrive with a problem, compare what they see, and leave the moment the value becomes difficult to understand.</p><p>Our job is to make the right business easier to choose. That means sharp positioning, human copy, distinctive design, dependable development, and a next step that feels proportionate to the trust already earned.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="wrap studio-principles section-space"><div class="sticky-copy"><SectionLabel>THE THINGS WE COME BACK TO</SectionLabel><h2>A point of view.<br/><span class="muted">In the details.</span></h2></div><div class="principle-list">{principles.map(([number, heading, description]) => <article class="value-card" data-reveal><span>{number}</span><h3>{heading}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div></section>
  <section class="studio-collaboration"><div class="wrap"><SectionLabel>WHAT IT FEELS LIKE TO WORK TOGETHER</SectionLabel><div class="collaboration-grid"><h2>You bring the truth about the business.<br/><em>We turn it into leverage.</em></h2><div><p>You do not need a polished brief. Bring the sales questions you answer every week, the clients you want more of, the proof you are proud of, and the part of the current journey that frustrates you.</p><ul><li>A diagnosis before a list of deliverables</li><li>A clear reason behind important decisions</li><li>Direct feedback from both sides</li><li>A scope tied to the bottleneck we are solving</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Tell us what is getting stuck <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={18}/></a></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="wrap studio-crossroads section-space"><a href="/work"><SectionLabel>THE THINKING, IN PRACTICE</SectionLabel><h2>Explore<br/>the work.</h2><Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={40}/></a><a href="/services"><SectionLabel>WHAT WE BRING TO THE TABLE</SectionLabel><h2>Meet the<br/>capabilities.</h2><Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={40}/></a></section>
  <ContactBanner />
</main>
</BaseLayout>
